knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3686
What it fixes: `images.loaderFile` in next.config was silently ignored on the
vinext target, so a custom image loader configured that way was never used
(the Next.js deploy tests next-image-new/loader-config and
next-image-new/loader-config-edge-runtime fail their loaderFile cases).
This patch ports the loaderFile half of the upstream PR: the vinext plugin
aliases the `vinext/shims/image-loader-file` slot to the user's file
(validated like Next.js: it must exist, and `images.loader` must be unset,
"default" or "custom"), `next/image` is served by a new `image-external`
shim that applies that loader to every image, and `images.loader: "custom"`
without a loader now throws Next.js's missing-loader error.
Companion: this is the second half of the #3686 port; the first half (the
trailingSlash path and per-width custom-loader srcSet) is
vinext-3686-image-trailingslash-loader-srcset.patch, which MUST apply first
(this patch's image.js hunks sit on top of it). It is a separate file so an
install that already carries the first half still applies cleanly.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3686.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

